## Made
I didn't really get a lot of time to work on projects this month (though I've got a couple
interesting ones in the pipeline for July onwards). Mostly it boiled down to:
* A couple small bugfixes in [thoth](https://codeberg.org/garrettm/thoth) for stupid edgecases I neglected to test.
* A tweak or two to the trusty dotfiles, mostly to do with `jj` on my work machine (where
I get the most mileage out of having nice aliases).

I did, however, reassemble my [Lego Blacksmith](https://www.lego.com/en-us/product/medieval-blacksmith-21325) set
that I brought to the Netherlands with me in a couple freezer bags 2.5 years ago. It now
sits proudly on my bookshelf next to the [Lunar Lander](https://www.lego.com/en-us/product/nasa-apollo-11-lunar-lander-10266) as a bookend.

# Stuff I Only Sorta Did or Didn't Do
Didn't run as much as I should, yadda yadda. Nothing really for this section this month
since I knew going in that June was going to be a big month for travel, and then the tail
end of it was taken over by the generational (or at this point, yearly) heatwave that hit
Europe. All good! Now that I'm back home and staying on this side of the Atlantic for the
foreseeable future, I can really kick it into gear.

# Stuff I'm Gonna Do in June
I've decided to try something new for this month and waaaaaay overdo it on the goals, with
the preliminary acceptance that it's OK if I'm not perfect on everything. But I figure I
may as well have a bunch of stuff to shoot for, especially with the summer in full swing:
* I want to try to listen to 3 full albums a week, but just listening. I listen to lots of
music at work or at home while I'm doing other things, but as I am starting to become a
Vinyl Guy :tm:, I want to make the effort to just enjoy some of the music I own for the
art of it. Dunno how I'll randomize it yet, but I wanna make the effort to do it.
* In the music vein, I want to practice guitar every day, just for 10 minutes. I'm really
inconsistent with my guitar practice, I tend to pick it up and noodle for a week and then
leave it sit for 2-3. I'd like to just get in the habit of playing it a bit every day,
even if I'm not actively learning a song.
* Now that I'm on the other side of my vacation (or at least the one where it was a bit of
a stretch to be super active at the same time), I want to super focus in on sticking to my
marathon training plan. I really want that 3:30 in October. Some of this is dependent on
the knee pain I mentioned above, but I'm starting to do more strength training and
stretching as well to help on that front.
* I want to watch one new movie a week. I have a list of films in my notes that I'll
occasionally pull from, and I want to try and replace some of the youtube or twitch that I
watch with actual full movies with like a plot and artistry and stuff. If I'm gonna watch
something, it may as well be a film and not just a random stream.
* Repeating a goal from [February](2026-feb), I wanna try and make one new dish a week.
Unlike February though, I'm not going to choose a random country this time around (I
think that added a bit too much of a hurdle and stress on finding ingredients). Instead
I'm going to choose something that I like to eat at a restaurant, and try and make that
at home (within reason). Also aiming to do mostly vegetarian stuff, because I ate so, so
much red meat in the US. I need to flush out the system.

Big month coming up! Lots of other stuff going on that I keep off the blog too, but I'm
generally in a good mood and getting out of the heatwave funk.
